sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.52" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.515"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Under the finite-encoding condition the book emphasizes, computable analysis already proves that many ordinary continuous models stay within Turing computation, and that literature is public. The claim also bundles practical analog machines and every idealized continuum, and those pieces do not share one theorem. Dropping the encoding condition is a known way to write equations that look more powerful, so the test is only as strong as the assumption." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Fix finite discrete encoding of inputs and outputs. Within that constraint, confirm the claim if analog machines, standard continuous equations, and idealized continuous models only compute Turing-computable functions; refute it by a continuous model, meeting the constraint, that decides a non-recursive set." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Reasonable assumptions do the real work: exact real oracles or infinite-time supertasks can exceed Turing computation if the assumption is dropped.", "Historical analog computers being slower than digital computers does not by itself bound idealized continuous models." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch12-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.55"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-08--grok--operationalizability> .
